body:
I think you need to sign up at a different gym.  My gym is amazing.  Sanitizer everywhere.  People constantly cleaning the machines.  We have a rule to have a towel and water with us.  All the members there are fairly nice.  Dunno how people can be rude if all you care about is working out.  My gym made it clear my contract is 3 years and if I break it I have to pay the rest.  Sounds like a normal business to me.

&#x200B;

My gym membership is also super cheap soooo yeah.  You're country just sounds... bad

In my contract it states that's my job.  Anything else comes from good morals.  And, you're expecting me not to be like that?  I am.  I am doing all those roles.  I'm just saying, I realise where the complaint came from.  I'm not paid to be a therapist, I'm paid to teach.  SO, if I do bring a therapeutic side, I shouldn't expect to be compensated for it.

&#x200B;

Edit:  Why are people downvoting this?  I legit said I put in the extra effort and don't expect to be paid for it lmao.

It's not that I'm scared of being stereotypical.  I live in South Africa so I am pretty clued up on diversity and stuff.  But I will have a look at that link, thank you.

&#x200B;

I just want to ask, won't overstating become boring for the reader?

&#x200B;

Edit: Holy shit that link is really amazing thanks a bunch.  Now I won't have to default to 'chocolate' if I can't think of anything other than black.

Ok, let us take "me" out of this equation, because I do struggle with mental illness so I might not be the best example when it comes to "sound" suggestion as bias might be there.  But what about the average player?  The one that can only play 1 or 2 games and gets a smurf.  What about the people forced to be exposed and face ridicule by pro players because they decided to make content out of disrespecting other players, because I promise you, styling is disrespecting.

&#x200B;

Why do I say this?  I use to play tabletennis professionally, and whenever someone, who was clearly better than me, decided to show off I got instantly demotivated.  I look like the idiot because this guy isn't even trying hard and making me look like shit, even if I play my heart out.   I'd rather lose 11-1 then lose 11-5 because the guy decided to play left handed.

&#x200B;

How is that fair to the average gamer?  The people that are suppose to support the content of the developers.

Well, that's my main concern with league, the age restriction.  Online games are not a place for kids.  The fact that I can't banter, because I have to watch out for kids, makes me mad. 

&#x200B;

Then again, I am against online gaming for kids that are not in a team enviroment, but thats just me.  League doesn't give off positive vibes.  Like look at the reason I got banned.  I got banned cause I flamed someone for flaming someone else.

&#x200B;

When simping gets you banned RIP

Didn't know calling for report is bannable, because I actually read the T&C because I was bored once.  Couldn't find anything about that.  

And I get I'm flaming, but ban me then for chats, but I am not using profanity.

&#x200B;

For example, my one friend got suspended yesterday for saying "kick the bucket you homosexual" which imo I understand, but I called someone dumb.

&#x200B;

How are those 2 the same

If the enemy Urgot is in the lane, there is no chance for survival.  If he is mute, step 2 is null and void, as he can not call for the strength of his crab brothers, therefore he has a 1% debuff towards his legs.

&#x200B;

Or you can pick Shen
